 "notes": "DESI Y1 stacked-spectra search for narrow optical emission lines from two-photon dark matter (ALP) decay. Headline result is Fig.8 (gamma_comp_update.pdf), bounds on the two-photon decay rate Gamma [s^-1] vs particle mass m [eV], with two this-work curves: BGS-5sigma (black, ~2.76-8.28 eV) and LRG-5sigma (green, ~3.55-12.4 eV). Converted to g_agamma using the papers Eq.5, Gamma=g_agamma^2 m_a^3/(64 pi) (natural units; identical to the canonical axion-photon decay rate), via g[eV^-1]=sqrt(64 pi hbar Gamma[s^-1]/m^3), g[GeV^-1]=g[eV^-1]*1e9, hbar=6.582e-16 eV s. Reported curve is the lower envelope (strongest, i.e. smallest g) of BGS and LRG at each mass; step near 8.3 eV is where BGS ends and only LRG continues. Vector curves extracted with pymupdf get_drawings (BGS path idx135 black, LRG idx136 green(0,0.5,0)); axes: x linear m 4/6/8/10/12 eV at 33.25 px/eV, y log 10^-29..10^-25 at 61.875 px/decade. Limits are 5-sigma detection limits (not 90/95% CL; confidence_level set null). Bound depends on assumed DM surface mass densities from SDSS/BOSS weak lensing (Sigma~70 Msun/pc^2 BGs, 145 Msun/pc^2 LRGs at 10 arcsec), not a local halo GeV/cm^3 density, so dm_density_assumed=null; shaded bands = 30% surface-density systematic (not included).",
